====Usage notes====
* Russian "[[pirozhki]]" ({{l|ru||пирожки́}}) and "[[pirogi]]" ({{l|ru||пироги́}}) and Polish [[pierogi]] (diminutive: "pierożki") (dumplings) are often confused. The two dishes are quite different. See [[pelmeni]] for the Russian version of the Polish [[pierogi]]. In certain regions of the Ukraine, these terms (пироги́, пиріжки́) may refer to either the Polish "pierogi" or the Russian "pirozhki".

